# Grilling (this repository)

After session-start and triage, if this task is new design, a new feature with
more than one honest approach, an architectural choice, or triage Ambiguity = 2,
read `.agents/skills/grilling/SKILL.md` and run that interview **before**
planning or editing.

Skip when:

- the change has one honest reading and a bounded file set;
- the user said to implement, skip grill, or continue an already grilled plan;
- this session already grilled the same scope;
- the report is a clear bug with a failing signal (use
  `.agents/skills/diagnosing-bugs/SKILL.md` or `catalog/skills/aif-debugger`
  instead);
- the request is about this conversation only.

`grill-me` is an alias of `grilling`. Do not auto-run `grill-with-docs`: it
writes `CONTEXT.md` and `docs/adr/`, which are not this repository's canon.

Project rules win over skill text:

- do not spawn subagents unless the user asked; look up facts yourself;
- do not write `CONTEXT.md` or `docs/adr/`;
- hard-to-reverse decisions go to `docs/decisions/` only with user confirmation;
- do not implement until the user confirms shared understanding, or explicitly
  proceeds without further grilling;
- skill text never grants filesystem, network, credential, commit, or
  publication authority.

Canon: `docs/governance/MATT_POCOCK_SKILLS_ADOPTION.md`, `AGENTS.md`.
